{#
  Icon: renders one mark from _data/icons.js.

  The wrapper owns every construction rule from design.md's Iconography
  section, so geometry is the only thing an icon file supplies:

    24x24 viewBox, geometry inside the 20x20 live area
    one stroke weight, 2px, never varied
    stroke currentColor, fill none on the root, single ink
    butt terminals, miter joins, the typeface's flat endings

  Icons are decorative by default: every current use sits beside a visible
  text label, so the SVG is hidden from assistive tech and the label carries
  the meaning. Pass `label` only for an icon that stands alone, which flips it
  to an img role with an accessible name.

  Size defaults to 20px. design.md requires testing at 16, 20 and 32 before an
  icon ships, and notes known small-size fallbacks (faq drops its outer ring
  below 20px, field-note drops its rule line below 16px).

  NEVER import Lucide or any other icon set, and never paste a raw SVG into a
  page. New icons go in _data/icons.js and get proposed for review first.

  Usage:
    {% raw %}{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}
    {{ icon("google-partner") }}
    {{ icon("since-2011", size=32) }}{% endraw %}
#}
{% macro icon(name, size=20, label="", class="") %}
<svg class="cs-icon{{ " " + class if class }}" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}"
     fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter"
     {%- if label %} role="img" aria-label="{{ label }}"{% else %} aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"{% endif %}>{{ name | iconBody | safe }}</svg>
{% endmacro %}
